First, from the screenshots and repro it’s clear the “tall” headers which are sortable are not vertically centering their text and icon in the cell — the other (non-sortable) headers use a plain `<span>` and the built‐in CSS centers them, but the sortable headers wrap their label in a `<button>` which by default is not a flex container, so in a taller row its contents sit up at the top.  

**Root cause:**  
In `TableHeader.js` the sortable path wraps its children in a plain `<button>` but never turns that button into a flex container or applies any vertical alignment, so when the row height increases (size="tall") the label+icons float to the top instead of centering.

**Fix:**  
Make the `<button>` a flex container and vertically center its contents. We can do this by adding an inline style (or new class) to the `<button>`.

Here is a single *SEARCH/REPLACE* patch in `packages/react/src/components/DataTable/TableHeader.js` to add `style={{ display: 'flex', alignItems: 'center' }}` to the sortable‐header `<button>`:

